  "verbalization": "Leosibirone B, (rel)- is shown to have a target relationship with CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including (1R,8S,9R,16R)-8,16-bis(4-hydroxyphenyl)-9-[(1R,8S,9R,16R)-4,6,12-trihydroxy-8,16-bis(4-hydroxyphenyl)-15-oxatetracyclo[8.6.1.02,7.014,17]heptadeca-2(7),3,5,10(17),11,13-hexaen-9-yl]-15-oxatetracyclo[8.6.1.02,7.014,17]heptadeca-2(7),3,5,10(17),11,13-hexaene-4,6,12-triol, (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan, and 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide. All these compounds are linked to ZR-75-1, suggesting a potential mechanism of action through the inhibition of a sialyltransferase enzyme. The evidence supports a pathway where Leosibirone B, (rel)- may act by targeting this enzyme, which is a key component in the biosynthesis of sialic acid, and thus influencing the expression or function of ZR-75-1. The final score indicates a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, but further validation would be needed to confirm the exact mechanism and the role of the sialyltransferase in ZR-75-1's function.",
